<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Black Sea Coastal Line</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1854</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> Coastal Line was a chain of Russian forts built from the late 1830s along the Black Sea coast of Circassia, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anapa">Anapa</a> towards Abkhazia, to cut the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a> off from Ottoman trade and supplies. Its isolated garrisons suffered heavily from disease, and in 1840 Circassian forces stormed several forts. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> abandoned the line in 1854 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a>.</p></div>
